w['worldLore']['The Crucible — Cups and Competitor Life']={'text':'The Eternal Crucible hosts voluntary individual championships with changing fields, named cup traditions and physically different arenas. First Bloom Cup, Highsun Clash, Harvest Crown and Frostglass Championship are sporting names, not promises that a particular season is currently underway. Entry terms and actual fields are announced. A loss ends the title run, but not a person\'s place in arena life. Competitors can talk, practice and learn between editions; ordinary sparring is not a championship.'}
w['worldLore']['The Crucible — Care and Sporting Boundaries']={'text':'Regulated bouts are nonlethal contests of actual subdual, surrender and referee decisions. Finite learned summons are permitted; outside assistance is not. Officials offer appropriate care or rest afterward. An unharmed fighter needs no invented wound and can continue without a compulsory medical scene. Mana potions and external stored-mana reserves are prohibited during active competition; normal control catalysts remain legal. A closed championship has a real champion and does not restart because somebody wants another final.'}
w['traits']['Oni']['description']=w['traits']['Oni']['description'].replace('or invented homeland','or compulsory homeland loyalty')
w['traits']['Oni']['traitNarrativeEffects']=w['traits']['Oni']['traitNarrativeEffects'].replace('or invented homeland','or compulsory homeland loyalty')+' The established homeland has Edo-inspired towns, fields, samurai and shinobi traditions with selected Arcane/Soul magitech. Ancestry alone grants none of those skills or affinities.'

story_ai=w['aiInstructions']['generateStory']
story_ai['Victory and Downtime']='Let actual success and loss stand. Preserve defeated foes, completed work, ownership and paid rewards until something really changes. Give aftermath room for relief, embarrassment, company, appropriate treatment and recovered belongings. Quiet play matters: meals, shopping, lessons, dates, work and festivals need no compulsory disaster or messenger. Do not interrupt a chosen confession, grief, reconciliation or rest unless an established cause truly intrudes. A requested long rest can pass its real interval with actual recovery; it does not cure irreparable injuries. Workers and friends keep their own plans. Staying can develop an activity; leaving respects the route. Refusal of content earns no arbitrary punishment.'
story_ai['Relevance and Source Scope']='Current state owns geography and outcomes; character records own identity and knowledge; local lore owns place; an active quest owns its agreed scope. Recent features do not dominate unrelated scenes. Keep private motives, flags, filenames, reward recipes and generation instructions out of public description and speech. Preserve ordinary lives and quiet scenes.'
story_ai['Crucible Activity']='At the Eternal Crucible, distinguish visitors, friendly sparring and the registered championship. Use the announced opponent, real arena and recorded result; never invent another final, reverse a knockout into victory or award a second prize. Bouts are actual nonlethal subdual with surrender and referee stops. After a settled bout, medics may offer appropriate care or rest once. If unharmed, do not invent injury; the fighter can continue. Treatment is optional, and readiness needs no exact Health/Mana/Stamina percentage. Conversation and teaching do not need a trigger for every exchange. Finite summons are legal; outside companions do not add attacks, buffs or healing. Let opponents have interests and flaws beyond the bracket. A semantic ruling can settle surrender or a disputed stop, but a player\'s boast alone proves no win.'
w['aiInstructions']['generateNPCIntents']['Crucible Sporting Intent']='A registered Crucible bout is actual regulated nonlethal subdual, not a merely discussed spar. Only its actual competitors and finite legal summons participate. Respect surrender, incapacity and referee stoppage immediately; no queued extra attack after the end. Outside companions, spectators, medics and announcers do not attack or supply live-bout buffs. Show the actual arena\'s cover and routes. Do not invent a lethal aim or a guaranteed harmless hit contrary to Combat Results.'
w['aiInstructions']['generateActionInfo']['Crucible Intent']='In a regulated Crucible bout, preserve actual nonlethal subdual intent and its real participants. Readiness is not an attack. Treat attacks and defenses as real resolved attempts; do not turn an invitation, status request or clinic visit into combat. Surrender, ring-out and referee decisions need the actual current bout, not an old result. An unharmed competitor may skip care. No exact resource-percentage gate governs entry.'
w['aiInstructions']['generateEncounters']['custom']=w['aiInstructions']['generateEncounters'].get('custom','')+'\nSepulchral Conservatory: register finite local guardian types before attacks. The Portal House is safe. Preserve cleared routes; conscious spirits and empty frames differ.'
# Preserve reserved spell/creation rules; do not add general acquisition gates.
w['death']['instructions']+='\nRegulated Crucible bouts preserve their actual nonlethal intent. A genuine tournament knockout is a sporting loss, not a newly invented lethal event. Capture the loss before describing treatment or recovery; healing never changes the result.'

